---
[v2] net: pcs: mtk-lynxi: add autoneg off mode

OpenWrt 24.10/25.12 enforces SFP optical modules to operate with autoneg
disabled in kernel 6.6/6.12, configured from user space via ethtool.

Without this patch, 1000BaseX SFP optical modules cannot successfully link
with their link partners.
---
v2: Refactor SGMII/1000BaseX autoneg off mode based on the backport of new
    phylink_mii_c22_pcs_decode_state().
v1: Add SGMII/1000BaseX autoneg off mode.
v3 (6.12.117 rebase): drop the get_state() hunk; the link_poll mechanism in
    999-pcs-07 rewrites that function entirely. Only the SGMSYS_SGMII_MODE
    mask change remains.
---

From f57c3c1318c7cf95c3fb0d0edc5bc38ad4d6f917 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bo-Cun Chen <bc-bocun.chen@mediatek.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Sep 2025 16:31:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: mtk-lynxi: add autoneg off

---
 drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-lynxi.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-lynxi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-lynxi.c
@@ -274,8 +274,8 @@
 	/* Update the sgmsys mode register */
 	regmap_update_bits(mpcs->regmap, SGMSYS_SGMII_MODE,
 			   SGMII_TRXBUF_THR_MASK |
-			   SGMII_REMOTE_FAULT_DIS | SGMII_SPEED_DUPLEX_AN |
-			   SGMII_IF_MODE_SGMII,
+			   SGMII_REMOTE_FAULT_DIS | SGMII_DUPLEX_HALF |
+			   SGMII_SPEED_DUPLEX_AN | SGMII_IF_MODE_SGMII,
 			   SGMII_TRXBUF_THR(trxbuf_thr) | sgm_mode);
 
 	/* Update the BMCR */
